enableActionPolicies.t.sol
└── when permission is not enabled
│   └── it should revert with PermissionIdNotEnabled
└── when permission is enabled
    ├── when actionPolicies array is empty
    │   └── it should complete without changes
    └── when actionPolicies array is not empty
        ├── when policy is not registered in registry
        │   └── it should revert with PolicyNotRegistered
        └── when policy is registered in registry
            ├── when action target is valid
            │   ├── when action already has policies
            │   │   └── it should add new policies to existing action and emit events
            │   └── when action has no existing policies
            │       └── it should enable new action with policies and emit events
            └── when action target is invalid (e.g., address(0))
               └── it should revert